-- title:
--   Specialisation of j(q^{dℓ'}) as the q-th power of a cyclic-quotient j
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   **The semistable frame over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.** Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $(q:\overline{\mathbb Q})\in A.\mathrm{nonunits}$). Write $\kappa_A$ for the residue field of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the intermediate field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_A\,M'$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\kappa_A$, the field generated over $\kappa_A$ by `jqModC` and `jqNModC _ M'`, and let `hW` say that $W$ consists exactly of the places in `ssPlaces q M' κ_A`, that is those $w$ satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M' κ_A`. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of intermediate fields of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$: the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change (adjoin the coefficientwise images) of the full level-$M'$ modular function field lies inside $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}(q^2M',\,\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` for $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_A\,M'$: a valuation subring `integers` of the source whose preimage in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal of `integers` and which is compatible with reduction on $A$, a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders of functions with nonzero residue, and the scaling clause that every nonzero element can be multiplied by a constant so as to land in `integers` with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0$.`integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$.
--
--   **The local base.** Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, let $\pi_0\in k_0$ lie in $A$, and put $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (the Lean `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ Qbar)`). The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that it is Henselian, and that its residue field is algebraically closed; `hκ` says that every $a\in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Level and function field.** Let $\ell'$ be a prime with $\ell'\neq q$, $\ell'\ge 3$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$; let $\xi\in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity, with `hιξ` asserting the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$ which, by `hK`, equals the $k_0$-base change $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')$, the level-$H$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$; $K$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure making $A_0\to k_0\to K$ a scalar tower. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,\mathrm{jq}$, the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function.
--
--   **The rigid moduli frame.** The hypotheses `hℓ` and `hM` are the variable-change equivariance clauses: for every commutative $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and variable change $C$, a `LevelPData` $D$ which is an `IsLevelPStructure` for $W$ and $\ell'$ (equations at $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$, vanishing of $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell'}$ at $x_P$ and $x_Q$, and invertibility of the two independence elements) transforms into one for $C\bullet W$, and a polynomial $h$ with `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (the two-torsion kernel condition if $p^k=2$, otherwise the cyclic-generator kernel condition) transforms into `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`. Let $\mathcal G$ be a family of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras with invertible discriminant, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`: pointwise evaluation exists) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: the unit section is cut out by a homomorphism from the origin chart ring killing `xOverY` and `zOverY`), and let $\mathcal T$ be a `LevelTransport` for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ (functorial transport of raw Drinfeld pairs along algebra maps and variable changes, preserving the level condition), assumed to satisfy `IsSectionTransport`, the compatibility of the transported sections $P,Q$ with variable-change and coefficient morphisms of graded model rings. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` supply, for each projective Weierstrass curve over an $A_0$-algebra, graded ring homomorphisms between the model gradings realising a variable change (`IsVariableChangeHom`) respectively a coefficient map (`IsCoefficientHom`), each with the irrelevant-ideal inequality. Let $P_0$ be a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for $A_0$ and the level moduli datum of $\mathrm{rigidDataPow}\,A_0\,\ell'\,M'\,q\,h\ell\,hM\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$, the rigidification of the product of the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel component for $M'$, the level-$\ell'$ component and the Drinfeld $q$-level component: so $P_0$ consists of an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$, a universal point `univ`, and the property that every point over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of `univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra map $B_0\to T$.
--
--   **The Tate point.** Let $x_0$ be a point of this datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant `jOf x₀` has Laurent expansion $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$, and let $\mathrm{clC}:B_0\to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ be an $A_0$-algebra map which, by `hclC`, becomes $P_0.\mathrm{classify}\,x_0$ after composing with the inclusion of the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j=\mathrm{chartAlg}\,A_0\,K\,\{j\}$ into $K$. The hypothesis `hμ` states that there are a variable change $C$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ and a raw representative $r$ of the rigid data over $K$ (a curve with invertible discriminant, level object and level condition) such that: the class of $r$ is $x_0$; the scaling $C.u$ satisfies $C.u\,(2x+ 1/6)=2y+x$ where $(x,y)=\mathrm{cuspPoint}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(1,0)$, and $C.r=-1/12$, $C.s=-1/2$, $C.t=1/24$; the curve of $r$, pushed into $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$, equals $C\bullet \mathrm{tateBase}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$; for every prime $p\mid M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f$ from $k_0$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $F'$, the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ becomes the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` transform, along $C$ and the degree $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,v_p(M')$, of $\prod_a (X-\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,(q\ell')\,(\zeta^a)_1)$ over $1\le a\le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p\nmid a$; the level-$\ell'$ datum $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ becomes the variable change by $C$ of $\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q,0)\,(0,-q)$; and there are $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y\in K$ whose expansions are the four coordinates of the variable change by $C$ of $\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(\ell',0)\,(0,-\ell')$, such that the Drinfeld sections $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P$ and $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.Q$ pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`. Finally $\theta:\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0\to\kappa_A$ is a ring homomorphism compatible with the residue maps of $A_0$ and $A$ (`hθ`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ and $\psi$ an $A_0$-algebra map from that chart algebra to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$. Let $x$ be a raw representative of the rigid data over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0$ whose class is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\psi\circ\mathrm{clC}$, and assume that the affine curve of $x$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point: $q\cdot P=0$ implies $P=0$.
--
--   Then for every field $\Omega$ which is an algebra over $\kappa_A$, every place $V$ of $\Omega$ over $\kappa_A$, every ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}$ from the residue field of $V$'s valuation subring to $\kappa_A$ and every ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ to that valuation subring, subject to the five clauses: $\mathrm{res}$ splits the structure map of $\kappa_A$; on elements of $A_0$ the composite $\rho$ followed by the inclusion into $\Omega$ is $\theta$ of the residue, pushed into $\Omega$; $\mathrm{res}$ of the residue of $\rho(c)$ is $\theta(\psi(c))$ for all $c$; the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho(\mathrm{jChartFin}\,A_0\,K\,j)$ is transcendental over $\kappa_A$; and $\Omega$ is finite-dimensional over $\kappa_A$ adjoined with that image —
--
--   and then, for every $A_0$-algebra structure on the valuation subring of $V$, every $A_0$-algebra map $\rho_A:B_0\to V$'s valuation subring with $\rho_A(b)=\rho(\mathrm{clC}\,b)$, every raw representative $x_V$ over that valuation subring whose class is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\rho_A$, every ring homomorphism $\chi_Q$ from the origin chart ring of the curve of $x_V.\mathrm{level}.2.2$ to $\Omega$ such that the morphism induced by the structure map of $\Omega$ followed by the section $Q$ of $x_V.\mathrm{level}.2.2$ equals the morphism induced by $\chi_Q$ followed by `originChartι`, with $\chi_Q(\mathrm{xOverY})=0$ and $\chi_Q(\mathrm{zOverY})=0$;
--
--   and for every $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma(\ell')$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{00}\equiv 0$ and $\gamma_{11}\equiv 0 \pmod q$, every $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ (on ratios of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H$ with integral $q$-expansions, $\tau$ realises the weight-$k$ slash action by the conjugate of $\gamma^{-1}$ at level $q\ell'$, after any embedding of $k_0$ in $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$), such that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra (`hpres`), and such that (`hTR`) for every element $h$ of the chart algebra all of whose Laurent coefficients of $\tau h$ lie in the maximal ideal of $A_0$ one has $\rho(h)=0$ in $\Omega$;
--
--   and for every nonzero $d\mid M'$ such that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'\,(\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb Q\,d\,\mathrm{jq}))$ — the series $j$ in the variable raised to the power $d\ell'$ — lies in $K$ and, as an element of $K$, lies in the chart algebra;
--
--   and for every algebraically closed field $\Lambda$ which is an $A_0$-algebra, every ring homomorphism $\iota:\Omega\to\Lambda$, every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi:B_0\to\Lambda$ with $\varphi(b)=\iota(\rho_A(b))$, with $M'\neq 0$ in $\Lambda$, every raw representative $x_\Lambda$ over $\Lambda$ whose class is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\varphi$, and every point $g$ of the affine curve of $x_\Lambda$ such that $g$ has exact order $M'$ and, for each prime $p\mid M'$, each $n$ and each nonsingular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n\cdot g=(x_1,y_1)$ and $n\cdot g$ of exact order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the polynomial $x_\Lambda.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ vanishes at $x_1$:
--
--   the image under $\iota$ of $\rho$ applied to that element of the chart algebra equals
--   $$\iota\bigl(\rho(\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'\,(\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb Q\,d\,\mathrm{jq})))\bigr)=\bigl(\mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}\,(x_\Lambda.\mathrm{curve})\,(\mathbb Z\cdot((M'/d)\cdot g))\,d\bigr)^{q},$$
--   where $\mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}\,V\,H\,N$ denotes $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the quotient curve $V.\mathrm{cyclicQuotientCurve}\,H\,N$.
--
--   On a branch of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $H$, this identifies the specialisation of the function $j(q^{d\ell'})$ at a supersingular point as the $q$-th power of the $j$-invariant of the quotient of the specialised elliptic curve by the cyclic subgroup of order $d$ generated by $(M'/d)g$; the $q$-th power records the Frobenius twist produced by the level automorphism $\tau$ attached to an antidiagonal-mod-$q$ element $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell')\cap\Gamma_0(M')$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_curve_reduction_eq_map_frobenius_cyclicQuotientJ_eq_of_levelAut_of_originChart_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_curve_reduction_eq_map_frobenius_cyclicQuotientJ_eq_of_levelAut_of_originChart_of_tatePoint) in the analysis of the reduction of the modular curve at $q$ that underlies the level-lowering step.
